msgid "Learning about services - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:19
msgid ""
"Services let nodes request data or trigger behavior only when needed. In "
"this article, you will use turtlesim and command-line tools to list, "
"inspect, call, and echo ROS services. After you follow these steps, you will "
"understand how service clients, servers, request types, and response types "
"work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:27
msgid "**Goal:** Learn about services in ROS 2 using command line tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:29
msgid ""
"Services are one of the communication types used to exchange data in a ROS "
"system. This article walks you through using command-line tools to examine "
"and call services between nodes. A hands-on exercise with Turtlesim helps "
"you understand how the call-and-response model works in the ROS graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:35
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:38
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:40
msgid ""
"Services use a call-and-response model: a client sends a request to a "
"server, which processes it and returns a response. Unlike topics, services "
"only provide data when specifically called, so they are not suited for "
"continuous data streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:43
msgid ""
"For more information, see :doc:`How ROS works <../../../../How-ROS-Works>`."
msgstr ""

