msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:311
msgid "Try the following command on the ``/clear`` service's type, ``Empty``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:313
msgid "$ ros2 interface show std_srvs/srv/Empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:319
msgid "---"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:323
msgid ""
"The ``---`` separates the request structure from the response structure. The "
"``Empty`` type doesn't send or receive any data, so its structure is blank "
"above and below the separator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:326
msgid ""
"Let's introspect a service with a type that sends and receives data, like ``/"
"spawn``. From the results of ``ros2 service list -t``, we know ``/spawn``'s "
"type is ``turtlesim_msgs/srv/Spawn``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:329
msgid ""
"To see the request and response arguments of the ``/spawn`` service, run:"
msgstr ""

