msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:337
msgid ""
"float32 x\n"
"float32 y\n"
"float32 theta\n"
"string name # Optional.  A unique name will be created and returned if this "
"is empty\n"
"---\n"
"string name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:346
msgid ""
"The text above the separator lists the arguments needed to call ``/spawn``: "
"``x``, ``y`` and ``theta`` determine the 2D pose of the spawned turtle, and "
"``name`` is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:349
msgid ""
"The text below the separator line is the response. In this case, the "
"response is the name assigned to the new turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:353
